---
description = "Race two revisions, keep both, then resolve what you've read. A live multi-value register running watershed's compiled Gleam kernel."
---

## A list isn't a queue

`mv_register_values` returns a result containing a sorted `List(String)`. The order is for display, not priority. A fresh register reads `[]`; writing an empty string reads `[""]`. There's no delete hidden in that spelling.

Two concurrent writes of the same text still produce two entries. Don't deduplicate them and mistake that for causal agreement. A fresh write after observing both replaces both, even if its text is unchanged. The clock advances, though no visible-value event need fire.

## One typed field on the sequenced stream

The JavaScript facade's ensure callback returns an `MvRegister` handle. Ensure waits for synchronization before looking up or creating the field; it doesn't make the next user write wait for acknowledgement. The read below includes that optimistic write. On the BEAM, `watershed_beam` has the corresponding typed API with blocking ensures and subject subscriptions.

