```

## Or let the peers exchange revisions

A CRDT document can use this register as its root. Connect with this configuration, then use the document delivered by a successful readiness callback. If you're filling a missing default rather than handling a user edit, wait for readiness and inspect the synchronized value first: an early seed can become a concurrent alternative.

{data-snippet="mv-register-p2p"}
```gleam
generated
```

## The merge example is a regression, too

This is the kernel test the suite runs, not a second merge implementation written for the page. A and B author independently, observe each other's alternatives, then A writes a combined revision. An unseen C would not be superseded: resolution covers only the history the writer observed.

{data-snippet="mv-register-concurrent-resolution"}
```gleam
generated
```

Return to the [MvRegister field sheet](/structures/registers#mv-register), or compare [RegisterCollection](/structures/registers#registers), which maintains atomic and last-write-wins views using server sequence numbers, and [PactMap](/structures/coordination#pact), which waits for a frozen quorum's protocol acknowledgements. None of those acknowledgements means a person approved a revision. Here, the application decides when and how to offer a resolving write.
